WEBVTT

00:00:00.432 --> 00:00:03.666
Lolly Inclusive Design Policy

00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:08.693
Last updated: 30 July 20 26

00:00:09.627 --> 00:00:11.668
Our ethos.

00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:15.739
An open source community includes all of

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.793
us.

00:00:17.585 --> 00:00:20.055
Software that anyone can read, run and

00:00:20.115 --> 00:00:23.054
change only earns that openness when

00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:25.836
anyone can actually use it - whatever they

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:29.244
see, hear, process, speak or believe.

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:32.965
So we treat accommodation as a form of

00:00:33.045 --> 00:00:36.542
celebration, never a compromise: a

00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:38.667
preference that makes Lolly calmer,

00:00:38.727 --> 00:00:41.641
louder, larger or more familiar for

00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:44.405
someone is not a degraded mode of the

00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:45.669
product.

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:49.413
It is the product, meeting one more of us

00:00:49.474 --> 00:00:51.019
where they are.

00:00:52.161 --> 00:00:54.666
What this policy covers

00:00:55.645 --> 00:00:59.087
Lolly is a creative tool: people come here

00:00:59.188 --> 00:01:01.894
to make things that represent them.

00:01:02.652 --> 00:01:05.355
That shapes every accommodation below in

00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:08.647
one specific way - adjusting the app never

00:01:08.707 --> 00:01:10.520
adjusts your work.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.143
Accessibility preferences restyle Lolly's

00:01:14.235 --> 00:01:17.912
own interface: menus, cards, navigation,

00:01:17.984 --> 00:01:19.019
type.

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:22.551
They are engineered never to reach inside

00:01:22.598 --> 00:01:26.344
the tool canvas or the export pipeline,

00:01:26.411 --> 00:01:29.573
and automated tests fail our builds if a

00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:32.529
preference could move a single pixel of an

00:01:32.607 --> 00:01:34.420
exported file.

00:01:35.193 --> 00:01:37.644
You should never have to choose between a

00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:41.020
comfortable app and a faithful render.

00:01:42.156 --> 00:01:43.928
Accessibility

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:58.425
Beyond following the platform's own signals «system dark mode, the OS reduced-motion preference», Lolly ships explicit, opt-in accessibility preferences on your profile:

00:01:59.164 --> 00:02:02.044
Reduce motion turns off transitions,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.480
slides and animated flourishes in the

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:12.200
app, and combines with «never overrides» your operating system's setting.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:17.850
Animated exports keep moving exactly as designed.

00:02:18.591 --> 00:02:21.514
High contrast strengthens borders, text

00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:24.494
and focus rings around your work.

00:02:25.287 --> 00:02:28.565
Your brand colours and canvas stay exactly

00:02:28.627 --> 00:02:30.344
as you set them.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.197
Large text grows the app's type and icon

00:02:34.258 --> 00:02:36.670
glyphs without reflowing your

00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:40.213
designs, so what you export is

00:02:40.278 --> 00:02:41.994
byte-identical.

00:02:42.754 --> 00:02:44.947
Hide colourful previews swaps the

00:02:45.008 --> 00:02:48.323
gallery's preview artwork for calm icon

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.909
and text cards, and softens project

00:02:51.984 --> 00:02:54.291
thumbnails, halving their colour and

00:02:54.352 --> 00:02:56.999
contrast, so they stay recognisable

00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:59.170
without the colour noise.

00:02:59.952 --> 00:03:02.533
Full colour returns the moment you step

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:05.340
inside a tool, so the one place

00:03:05.424 --> 00:03:08.401
high-stimulus imagery appears is the one

00:03:08.463 --> 00:03:11.244
place you chose to work on it.

00:03:12.016 --> 00:03:15.038
Alongside the preferences: controls carry

00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:17.245
accessible names and pressed states,

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:19.509
changes are announced to screen readers,

00:03:19.554 --> 00:03:22.063
overlays close on Escape, keyboard focus

00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:24.115
is visible and strengthened further under

00:03:24.175 --> 00:03:26.651
high contrast, and every one of these

00:03:26.711 --> 00:03:29.530
switches is a plain, always-visible card

00:03:29.561 --> 00:03:32.432
on the profile page - findable by someone

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:35.483
who can barely read the page as it is,

00:03:35.539 --> 00:03:38.095
which is the moment it matters.

00:03:38.889 --> 00:03:40.033
Listen.

00:03:40.806 --> 00:03:43.427
Every page of this documentation can be

00:03:43.488 --> 00:03:46.315
read aloud - play, pause, and follow the

00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:49.481
words as they are spoken, at a pace you

00:03:49.571 --> 00:03:50.545
set.

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:54.808
Slowing down costs nothing in quality: it

00:03:54.855 --> 00:03:57.362
is a different speed, not a lesser one,

00:03:57.444 --> 00:04:00.669
for anyone who learns at their own pace.

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:05.081
Reduced and enhanced stimulation

00:04:05.984 --> 00:04:09.184
Neurodivergent people are not one audience

00:04:09.241 --> 00:04:10.869
with one need.

00:04:11.639 --> 00:04:14.448
The same brain that is overwhelmed by a

00:04:14.538 --> 00:04:17.739
wall of colourful thumbnails on a hard day

00:04:17.836 --> 00:04:20.954
may seek strong sensory input on another,

00:04:21.044 --> 00:04:24.071
so Lolly accommodates in both directions,

00:04:24.135 --> 00:04:25.920
always opt-in:

00:04:26.696 --> 00:04:28.793
Turning it down.

00:04:29.572 --> 00:04:32.520
Reduce motion and Hide colourful previews

00:04:32.608 --> 00:04:33.731
strip the

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:39.600
interface back to icons, text and one accent colour.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:58.525
Navigation stays busy-free for people with ADHD, autistic people and dyslexic people who find dense, high-variance imagery hard to scan; nothing you need «favourites, pinning, actions» is taken away in the calmer presentation.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.118
Turning it up.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.845
Neurospicy Mode is a deliberate sensory

00:05:04.906 --> 00:05:06.391
layer - focus

00:05:07.363 --> 00:05:09.616
loops, an atmosphere mixer with

00:05:09.695 --> 00:05:12.382
individually levelled ambient beds,

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:14.877
procedural music and interface sound

00:05:14.913 --> 00:05:18.131
effects - for people who focus best with

00:05:18.212 --> 00:05:19.719
rich input.

00:05:20.478 --> 00:05:23.884
It is off by default and never auto-plays

00:05:23.945 --> 00:05:25.669
before you ask.

00:05:26.473 --> 00:05:28.818
Sound is separable.

00:05:29.581 --> 00:05:32.645
Every audible layer has its own switch, so

00:05:32.689 --> 00:05:33.845
"visuals

00:05:34.755 --> 00:05:38.248
calm, sound rich" and the reverse are both

00:05:38.322 --> 00:05:41.188
real configurations, not a single

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.918
accessibility bundle someone else composed

00:05:43.993 --> 00:05:45.245
for you.

00:05:46.399 --> 00:05:50.191
Language and localization priority

00:05:51.164 --> 00:05:54.209
Lolly's interface and documentation are

00:05:54.272 --> 00:05:57.516
translated into more than 25

00:05:58.554 --> 00:06:01.984
languages, and we prioritise languages by

00:06:02.045 --> 00:06:05.293
how many people speak them, not by market

00:06:05.362 --> 00:06:08.278
revenue - Hindi, Bengali, Urdu and

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.587
Indonesian arrived in the same waves as

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.544
French and German.

00:06:14.318 --> 00:06:16.908
Right-to-left scripts are first-class:

00:06:16.983 --> 00:06:20.369
Arabic ships with full RTL layout, not

00:06:21.304 --> 00:06:23.943
a mirrored afterthought.

00:06:24.739 --> 00:06:26.759
Languages are distinct, not

00:06:26.815 --> 00:06:30.079
interchangeable: Indonesian and Malay are

00:06:30.172 --> 00:06:31.070
separate

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.807
catalogs, Traditional and Simplified

00:06:34.869 --> 00:06:37.986
Chinese are separate catalogs, and the

00:06:38.048 --> 00:06:40.610
language attribute is set before first

00:06:40.672 --> 00:06:43.170
paint so Han characters and script

00:06:43.233 --> 00:06:45.704
fallbacks render correctly for your

00:06:45.766 --> 00:06:48.619
language, not a lookalike.

00:06:49.383 --> 00:06:51.985
The language menu lists every language in

00:06:52.017 --> 00:06:55.501
its own name and script, and can be

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.561
ordered by speaker population, so finding

00:06:59.623 --> 00:07:02.282
yours never requires knowing its English

00:07:02.343 --> 00:07:03.369
name.

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:06.556
Cultural inclusion

00:07:07.466 --> 00:07:10.055
The neutral starting brand assumes nothing

00:07:10.092 --> 00:07:13.235
about who you are; Lolly exists so

00:07:14.191 --> 00:07:16.973
your own identity, palette and type

00:07:17.022 --> 00:07:19.493
replace ours in minutes.

00:07:20.267 --> 00:07:23.561
Type is treated as a cultural surface:

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.652
uploaded and Google fonts are shaped

00:07:27.585 --> 00:07:30.647
with proper text shaping across scripts,

00:07:30.739 --> 00:07:34.169
so names, diacritics and non-Latin text

00:07:34.226 --> 00:07:37.223
export as correctly drawn outlines rather

00:07:37.285 --> 00:07:40.119
than tofu or substitutions.

00:07:40.879 --> 00:07:43.522
Copy avoids idioms and culture-bound

00:07:43.582 --> 00:07:46.747
references that translate poorly, and

00:07:47.731 --> 00:07:50.922
translators receive clean, bare strings

00:07:50.985 --> 00:07:53.330
rather than sentences with markup

00:07:53.395 --> 00:07:55.294
fragments baked in.

00:07:56.413 --> 00:07:59.023
Why this produces better work, not just

00:07:59.098 --> 00:08:00.594
kinder software

00:08:01.598 --> 00:08:04.714
Accessibility gets filed under compliance,

00:08:04.763 --> 00:08:08.169
which quietly frames it as a cost.

00:08:08.944 --> 00:08:11.018
It is not one.

00:08:11.784 --> 00:08:14.162
The same properties that make a tool

00:08:14.222 --> 00:08:17.368
usable on a hard day make it faster on

00:08:17.458 --> 00:08:20.570
every other day, and they compound.

00:08:21.343 --> 00:08:25.343
Cognitive endurance is the real budget.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:29.098
Attention is finite and it

00:08:30.102 --> 00:08:32.468
drains unevenly.

00:08:33.226 --> 00:08:36.102
Every dialog you dismiss, every setting

00:08:36.157 --> 00:08:38.905
that resets, every choice a template

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:41.462
should have made for you spends a little

00:08:41.514 --> 00:08:44.370
of what you had left for the work.

00:08:45.129 --> 00:08:47.695
Constraint-first tools spend almost none

00:08:47.728 --> 00:08:51.120
of it: the brand decisions were made once,

00:08:51.186 --> 00:08:53.990
at the tool, so producing the twentieth

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:56.844
asset costs what the first did.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.386
People who need that most feel it first,

00:09:00.444 --> 00:09:03.220
and everyone benefits from it.

00:09:03.983 --> 00:09:07.137
Creative confidence comes from a floor you

00:09:07.199 --> 00:09:09.019
cannot fall through.

00:09:09.814 --> 00:09:10.480
When

00:09:11.535 --> 00:09:14.129
any output could be wrong in a way you

00:09:14.187 --> 00:09:16.951
will only discover later, you check

00:09:17.045 --> 00:09:20.094
everything twice and stay cautious.

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:24.050
When off-brand output is not reachable,

00:09:24.112 --> 00:09:26.791
the checking stops being your job and the

00:09:26.864 --> 00:09:29.569
caution goes back into the work.

00:09:30.326 --> 00:09:33.508
Confidence is not a mood here, it is a

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:35.994
property of the constraints.

00:09:36.795 --> 00:09:38.768
Right compounds.

00:09:39.533 --> 00:09:42.797
A decision encoded in a tool is correct

00:09:42.897 --> 00:09:44.228
every time

00:09:45.125 --> 00:09:47.707
that tool runs, in every language, at

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:51.295
every size, for everyone who uses it.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.706
A decision written in a guidelines PDF is

00:09:55.768 --> 00:09:59.019
correct as often as it is read.

00:09:59.796 --> 00:10:02.680
The difference is small on one asset and

00:10:02.733 --> 00:10:05.268
enormous across a year.

00:10:06.054 --> 00:10:08.671
What protects the workflow protects the

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:09.944
person.

00:10:10.729 --> 00:10:13.193
On-device rendering,

00:10:13.961 --> 00:10:17.213
plain-file exports and offline capability

00:10:17.311 --> 00:10:20.526
are usually filed under privacy, and they

00:10:20.605 --> 00:10:23.324
are also what keeps you working on a bad

00:10:23.386 --> 00:10:26.643
connection, on a locked-down machine, or

00:10:26.698 --> 00:10:29.544
the day a subscription lapses.

00:10:30.327 --> 00:10:33.103
Your workflow does not have dependencies

00:10:33.195 --> 00:10:35.194
you did not choose.

00:10:35.973 --> 00:10:38.243
Two things follow that we treat as

00:10:38.301 --> 00:10:41.943
inseparable: operational superiority,

00:10:42.004 --> 00:10:44.065
because software that respects your

00:10:44.123 --> 00:10:47.086
attention and your data is simply faster

00:10:47.176 --> 00:10:50.235
to work in, and ethics that cannot be

00:10:50.297 --> 00:10:52.333
traded away, because they are

00:10:52.422 --> 00:10:55.269
architectural rather than promised.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.918
A policy can be revised under pressure.

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:03.870
An engine that never receives your content

00:11:03.937 --> 00:11:06.319
has nothing to revise.

00:11:07.457 --> 00:11:09.369
Ethical commitments

00:11:10.282 --> 00:11:13.143
Privacy by architecture.

00:11:13.958 --> 00:11:17.092
Your work stays on your device.

00:11:17.879 --> 00:11:19.376
There are no

00:11:20.353 --> 00:11:23.659
trackers or analytics in the codebase, and

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:26.733
the few network touchpoints are enumerated

00:11:26.793 --> 00:11:28.920
in the Privacy Policy.

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:32.604
Accessibility and language preferences are

00:11:32.691 --> 00:11:36.453
stored in your own profile, on your device

00:11:36.537 --> 00:11:39.365
- a person's disability or language is

00:11:39.452 --> 00:11:41.170
never telemetry.

00:11:41.935 --> 00:11:45.368
Telemetry is no friend of this project: we

00:11:45.407 --> 00:11:47.994
don't want it, and nobody should have to

00:11:48.054 --> 00:11:50.120
give their data away.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.893
Honest provenance.

00:11:53.654 --> 00:11:57.267
Exports can carry Content Credentials, and

00:11:58.302 --> 00:12:02.718
AI-generated content is labelled as such.

00:12:03.492 --> 00:12:06.413
We believe audiences deserve to know how

00:12:06.474 --> 00:12:10.130
media was made, and creators deserve tools

00:12:10.188 --> 00:12:13.020
that can prove their work is theirs.

00:12:13.832 --> 00:12:16.143
No dark patterns.

00:12:16.889 --> 00:12:19.583
Preferences are plain switches that do

00:12:19.644 --> 00:12:21.144
what they say,

00:12:21.525 --> 00:12:34.625
defaults are dormant until you choose them, and platform conventions «native scrolling, browser shortcuts, standard dialogs» are respected rather than hijacked.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.269
Open source.

00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:41.430
The engine, shells and community tools are

00:12:41.492 --> 00:12:42.619
public.

00:12:43.404 --> 00:12:44.063
Every

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.565
claim in this document is checkable in the

00:12:47.668 --> 00:12:51.229
source, and several are enforced by tests

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.558
that fail the build when broken - the

00:12:53.656 --> 00:12:56.495
additive-by-default rule for accessibility

00:12:56.556 --> 00:12:59.424
attributes, the ban on preferences

00:12:59.486 --> 00:13:02.533
reaching exports, and the keeping-in-step

00:13:02.566 --> 00:13:04.778
of the app's two copies of each

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.119
preference.

00:13:07.251 --> 00:13:09.906
Holding ourselves to it

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:20.750
Inclusive design here is a policy in the engineering sense: invariants with tests, not aspirations with adjectives.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:37.350
When an accommodation and a feature conflict, we redesign the feature «when a 'hide previews' setting also hid icons off utility cards, the fix was to keep the actions, not to excuse the loss».

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:48.850
If something in Lolly excludes you - a missing language, an overwhelming moment, an assumption we baked in without noticing - that is a bug.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:52.550
Tell us: fitzy@suse-com.
